      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x^2 + \\dfrac{1}{x^2} \\right) ^2 = \\left(x^4 + \\dfrac{1}{x^4} \\right) + 2\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x^2 + \\dfrac{1}{x^2} \\right) ^2 \\)</span>&nbsp;= 322 + 2 = 324</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x^2 + \\dfrac{1}{x^2} \\right) = 18 \\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x - \\dfrac{1}{x} \\right) ^2 = \\left(x^2 + \\dfrac{1}{x^2} \\right) - 2 \\)</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x - \\dfrac{1}{x} \\right) ^2 \\)</span>&nbsp;= 18 - 2 = 16</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x - \\dfrac{1}{x} \\right) \\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;&plusmn; 4</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The one value of&nbsp;</strong><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left(x - \\dfrac{1}{x} \\right) \\)</span><strong>&nbsp;is 4.</strong></p>\n",
